ithout slowing agent velocity: [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]every master commit gets its own uncancelled CI run, the release [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]gate reads only the fast per-SHA gate, the exhaustive suite still [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]runs on a cadence and still guards the release, and ci_watch merges[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]the release PR with the merge strategy the repository actually [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]allows.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]8[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]4[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]release_gate_liveness.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Fast per-SHA master gate[/bold #D7AFFF]                                      [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]gate[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]gate: add master-gate.yml — a per-SHA, never-cancelled push lane that [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]runs the whole fast suite in balanced shards plus the lint gate, gets [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the Rust core from a SHA-keyed wheel cache instead of a 9-minute source [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]build, and adds its README badge.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]ci_watch gating allowlist, heavy-lane freshness, and merge [/bold #D7AFFF]   [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]strategy[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]chop[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]chop: teach ci_watch a gating_workflows allowlist evaluated against [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]HEAD-scoped runs, add a heavy-lane green-and-fresh release condition, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]switch the release merge to the repository's allowed merge-commit [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]strategy, and cut a bugyi-chops release.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Scheduled heavy lane off the push path[/bold #D7AFFF]                        [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]heavy[dim] · [dim][/dim]after gate[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]heavy: make ci.yml pull-request-and-workflow_call only, add full.yml as [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]a scheduled caller carrying the exhaustive matrix, retire the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]flake-reproducer cron from the master push path, repoint the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]coverage-contexts consumer, and add the second README badge.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Throttle release-please to a schedule[/bold #D7AFFF]                         [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]throttle[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]throttle: move publish.yml's release-please and release-metadata [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]reconciliation from every master push onto a schedule plus [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]workflow_dispatch while keeping publishing prompt, closing the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]empty-rollup and generator-busy gate conditions.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Drive the master gate green[/bold #D7AFFF]                                   [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]green[dim] · [dim][/dim]after gate[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]green: use the new per-commit signal to attribute and fix every failure [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the gate reports until master is durably green, filing task beads for [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]flakes rather than muting them.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Pin the Rust core revision CI builds[/bold #D7AFFF]                          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]corepin[dim] · [dim][/dim]after gate, heavy[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]corepin: record a sase-core revision in-repo, build CI's core wheel from[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]that revision instead of unpinned HEAD, and add a ratchet path that [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]proposes bumps so a sase-core push can no longer redden sase master on [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]its own.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Chop configuration rollout[/bold #D7AFFF]                                    [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]config[dim] · [dim][/dim]after gate, chop, heavy[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]config: update the ci_watch chop's chezmoi configuration with the new [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]gating and heavy-lane variables, install the released plugin, and verify[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]a dry-run tick reports the expected reason.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Measure the acceptance criteria and ship v0.17.0[/bold #D7AFFF]              [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]verify[dim] · [dim][/dim]after green, throttle, corepin, config[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]verify: measure every acceptance criterion against live run data, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]confirm the release gate opened and the release published, and record [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]what remains deferred.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-um","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-um.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","role_suffix":"plan","vcs_provider":"GitHub","workflow_name":"sase-um.1"},"source_run_id":"run-6b83eff63f34d298b96b7d89d39488e6","started_at":"2026-08-27T11:10:07.355659+00:00","state":"completed"},{"commits":[{"committed_at":1787788155,"sha":"bee05929dd7104804fd9d13252da1789fcd6e2bb","subject":"ci(release): throttle release-please workflow"}],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"chat":{"digest":"989dda66de5090c942c74dfe336467269ad3e403363e6263aab1